#
# This repo has core.autocrlf=true as a common Windows dev default and,
# until now, no .gitattributes at all, which lets git "helpfully" convert
# LF to CRLF on checkout for anything it does not detect as binary by
# content sniffing. WASM files (magic bytes start with a NUL) are caught by
# that sniffing and survive; the JS glue files that ship alongside them are
# plain ASCII and are NOT, so they silently get CRLF-mangled on a Windows
# checkout, which breaks their SHA-384 SRI hash against integrity.json (the
# browser then refuses to load them as "possible tampering", correctly, on
# an artifact that was actually just checkout-mangled). Observed exactly
# this happening to already-committed vendor JS under
# meshchatx/src/frontend/public/assets/js/codec2-emscripten/ and
# meshchatx/src/frontend/public/rnode-flasher/js/ while working on this
# change; scoped here to the new lxmf-stamper-wasm vendor files rather than
# auditing every vendored asset in the repo.

meshchatx/src/frontend/public/vendor/lxmf-stamper-wasm/*.wasm binary
meshchatx/src/frontend/public/vendor/lxmf-stamper-wasm/*.js -text
